`references/flow_diagram.md`.

Rules for this file:
- One `###` section for EACH "Step-by-step Flow — ..." section in `design.md` (same name, same
  order). Do not merge several flows into one diagram, do not split one flow across several diagrams.
- Default is a **sequence diagram**. Add a **flowchart** only for branching logic that a sequence
  diagram draws awkwardly — e.g. a send-limit/lock state machine, a retry loop. The flowchart must
  point to the exact decision table/block in `design.md` and must not invent branches. See
  `references/flow_diagram.md` for a flowchart sample.
- A feature with exactly ONE query and no write (no Step-by-step Flow in `design.md`): **omit this
  whole file** — the "Request flow" section in `design.md` keeps its compact ASCII trace.
- Message/participant labels are short English text; Mermaid keywords (`participant`, `alt`,
  `loop`, ...) are English too (Language policy in CLAUDE.md). User-facing copy quoted in a label
  keeps its own language.
- Every `⚠️ Not confirmed` on a step in `design.md` appears here as a `Note` on the matching
  message — never drawn as if it were settled.
